===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er|more}}

# [[cranky|Cranky]], [[disagreeable]], or [[stubborn]], especially if prone to [[odd]] [[whim]]s or [[fancy|fancies]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1929|year_published=≥1956|author=William Faulkner|title=The Sound and the Fury|chapter=JUNE SECOND 1910|url=|page=184|text=&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;“and Gerald‘s grandfather always picked his own mint before breakfast, while the dew was still on it. He wouldnt even let old Wilkie touch it do you remember Gerald but always gathered it himself and made his own julep. He was as '''crochety''' about his julep as an old maid, measuring everything by a recipe in his head. There was only one man he ever gave that recipe to; that was”|publisher=The Modern Library}}

